Part of #137. Triggered on 2026-11-10: the product owner's \"Send me a test\" (#136) said \"Test sent\", but no email arrived. Production D1 \`email_message\` and \`test_invitation_index\` are empty (no email was ever accepted by Cloudflare from the app), while a direct \`cf email-sending send\` from \`team@notify.surveybeat.app\` is accepted. The reason is stored only in the Organization Durable Object's send states, which nobody can see.

## Acceptance criteria
- After "Send me a test", the Pulse editor shows the test send's live state (queued, sending, sent, failed with the reason code such as \`E_SENDER_NOT_VERIFIED\` or \`unknown\`), refreshing until it settles.
- Organization admins get a "Failed emails" list in Organization settings: the last 50 failed sends of any kind (kind, recipient, reason code, time), never any email body or token. Endpoint classified in \`PrivacyRegistry.ts\`.
- If the email queue consumer itself errors before reaching the send store (so no state changes), that is visible too: the send stays "queued" past a threshold and the UI says so.
- English and German copy; tests for each state.

